    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d686">

                <pb facs="0836" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg742"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Springer to Mr.
                            Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-11-12"><hi rendition="#italic">November 12,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 211.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have been informed by the sister of
                    Laborde, one of the <hi rendition="#italic">Competitor</hi> prisoners, that he
                    was yesterday afternoon, at the time of her weekly visit to him, seized with
                    cerebral congestion and removed to the old military hospital of this city.</p>
                <p>Charles Leavitt, another of the prisoners, was removed several days ago to the
                    same hospital, supposed to be ill with yellow fever, but it seems to be a sort
                    of prison fever, induced by confinement and insufficient food.</p>
                <p>Ona Melton, it is stated, is greatly reduced for the same reasons.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. A. Springer.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
